<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nizam al-Mulk</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">vizier 1064–1092; assassinated 1092</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nizam al-Mulk was a Persian statesman who served as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vizier">vizier</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuk Empire</a> from 1064 until his assassination in 1092. He fused Persian bureaucratic tradition with Turkic military rule, founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nizamiyya">Nizamiyya</a> network of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madrasa">madrasas</a> and wrote the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siyasatnama">Siyasat-nama</a>, a treatise on government. His death removed a central figure of Seljuk administration.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nizam-al-mulk.jpg" alt="Nizam al-Mulk" width="317" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Themanlonewolf · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nizam_Al-Mulk.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
